<title>USA: Toys &quot;R&quot; Us Inc Q3 net rises.</title>
<headline>Toys &quot;R&quot; Us Inc Q3 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>PARAMUS, N.J. 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.12		    $0.08</p>
<p> Net			 33,300		   20,800</p>
<p> Sales		  1,883,000		1,714,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 278,700		  275,200</p>
<p>	  Nine months</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.16		    $0.20</p>
<p> Net			 44,500		   55,100</p>
<p> Sales		  5,264,900		4,821,700</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 277,000		  277,800</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: Nine-month net and share figures include a $55 million second quarter charge for an arbitration award.  </p>
<p>First Call put Wall Street estimates at $0.11 per share for the third quarter.</p>
</text>
